<title>PERU: Peru says October sugar output off 0.43 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru says October sugar output off 0.43 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar production fell in October by 0.43 percent to 63,444 tonnes compared to the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry's report added that sugar output for the first ten months fell to 480,393 tonnes from 511,973 tonnes, compared to the same period last year.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 643,165 tonnes.</p>
<p>Previous October production figures issued by the Agriculture Ministry were for sugar cane.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
